WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:13.870
In 1980, the historical Medellin Cartel leader,
Pablo Escobar, had an idea.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:19.200
Basically, he had a vision, a dream: to turn
Colombia into a narco-state; a country where

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.480
the government and all public institutions
would be directly controlled by drug trafficking.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.610
Such was his commitment, that in 1982 – as...

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:32.070
I think you all know – Pablo Escobar himself,
one of the most important mobsters in all

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.730
of history, gained a seat at the Colombian
chamber of representatives.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:37.730
And...

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:42.900
it’s important to bear in mind that it’s
one thing for the Mafia to buy or bribe a

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:46.320
politician, and quite another for them to
hold all the power directly.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.230
Can you imagine a country where the police,
the army, all administrative officials and

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:56.030
even the courts themselves were ultimately
under the direct orders of drug-dealers?

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:00.079
Of course, if Pablo Escobar's vision had panned
out, Colombia wouldn’t only have much higher

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:04.250
levels of drug production and export, but
the Medellín Cartel itself would’ve become

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.240
untouchable, invincible....

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.159
He would’ve gained complete impunity to
do and undo whatever he wanted at will.

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:14.180
Fortunately, Pablo Escobar never managed to
carry out his dream...

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.180
However...

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.570
today, 3 decades later it looks like his dream
is now being realized; But... this time we

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:31.750
aren’t talking about Colombia, we’re talking
about Venezuela.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:42.990
Apparently, the four characters you’re looking
at right now…

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:47.240
Don’t only control the country, they are
also the leaders of an international crime

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.740
and drug trafficking network.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:52.479
Of course, we’re talking about:
Nicolás Maduro, President of Venezuela.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:57.060
Diosdado Cabello the powerful president of
the National Constituent Assembly, whom many

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.550
already rank as the strongest man in the regime.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:04.450
And Tareck El Aissami, former Vice President
and current Minister of Industry and National

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:09.450
Production, whose personal fortune, according
to DEA calculations, surpasses the 3 billion

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.450
dollar mark.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:11.450
3 billion dollars!

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:14.780
And, the fourth, is Néstor Reverol, minister
of Internal Affairs, Justice and Peace, who,

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.870
to top it off, was the previous National Counternarcotics
Office Director.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:23.480
Well, everything indicates that these four
people are leading the transformation of Venezuela

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.799
into a narco-state.

00:02:24.799 --> 00:02:31.069
Listen up.

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:35.529
THE MAFIA TAKES CONTROL

00:02:35.529 --> 00:02:36.700
Venezuela is in shreds.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.859
Hunger is increasing, inflation is out of
control and hundreds of thousands of people

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:42.019
are fleeing the country.

00:02:42.019 --> 00:02:46.409
Even hospitals don’t have basic supplies
like medicine, analytical equipment or plasters.

00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:51.040
There’s such a huge mess that the PDVSA
itself; the Venezuelan state-owned oil company

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.049
with the most reserves in the world, is bankrupt.

00:02:55.049 --> 00:02:57.489
Check this out...

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:02.739
To this day, PDVSA has so many embargo orders
that in order to sell the increasingly dwindling

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:06.879
Venezuelan oil, it’s beginning to resort
to tricks and techniques used by Hollywood

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:08.709
movie-style smugglers:

00:03:08.709 --> 00:03:14.309
For example, since Venezuelan oil companies
are at risk of being confiscated... to settle

00:03:14.309 --> 00:03:17.219
all outstanding debts on the oil they transport...

00:03:17.219 --> 00:03:22.340
PDVSA has begun to transfer oil from its ships
to other ships with the Cuban flag out at

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:26.989
sea… who are then responsible for taking
the crude oil to its destination, thus avoiding

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:28.329
being seized.

00:03:28.329 --> 00:03:35.299
Because folks, in Venezuela practically everything
that has value, has been or is being looted.

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:38.180
Corruption has reached almost every corner
of the country.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.790
Let's see, the Bolivarian revolution promised
prosperity...

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:45.219
what they forgot to clarify is that all that
prosperity would only be for a few... for

00:03:45.219 --> 00:03:47.049
the friends of the revolution, of course.

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:48.189
Don’t believe me?

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:51.569
Well, take a look…

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:56.879
Many regime members promote and lead operations
for gas contraband to sell in Brazil and Colombia.

00:03:56.879 --> 00:04:00.779
They are also mostly responsible for food
and medicine contraband, which the state buys

00:04:00.779 --> 00:04:02.449
and then sells on the black market.

00:04:02.449 --> 00:04:06.371
They have looted public accounts and tens
of billions of dollars have disappeared both

00:04:06.371 --> 00:04:10.819
from the government and from PDVSA.

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:14.290
In Venezuela, even the Central Bank’s US
dollars have been looted...

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.320
Yes, you heard that right.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.360
Allow me to explain.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:22.000
One of the first things that the Chavez regime
did was implement a rigid exchange control...

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.240
that fixed, for example, the official exchange
between the bolivar and the US dollar, to

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.330
a rate that had nothing to do with the numbers
on the street.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.860
That way, the government’s friends could
access US dollars with just a handful of bolivares.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:40.510
Bolivares that due to the country’s current
hyperinflation are now worth practically nothing.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:45.080
The maneuver was so well perfected, that it
is estimated that 20% of all imports declared

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:49.760
in recent years have been completely false
operations that were done for the sole purpose

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:54.720
of obtaining dollars at the official exchange
rate, to save them in foreign accounts.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:59.200
And, this is important, because according
to estimates we could be talking about a theft

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.510
of more than 100 billion dollars.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:06.890
And of course, PDVSA hasn’t escaped this
plunder:

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:14.120
(“A group of companies lent 7.2 billion
bolivares to PDVSA, which, when exchanged

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.750
at the black market rate, would be about 42
million dollars, but when exchanged at the

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:23.190
official rate, would become approximately
600 million dollars, which were deposited

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.530
in an account in Malta.”

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:25.530
César Batiz, Venezuelan journalist)

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:26.940
But of course...

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:32.530
since no more can be squeezed out of the country,
the regime giants have sought a new alternative

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:53.410
source 

00:05:53.410 --> 00:06:06.210
of income.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:21.000
(TURNING INTO A NARCO-STATE)

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.250
The issue of drug-dealers and Venezuela isn’t
new...

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.360
it has, however, evolved.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.450
Allow me to explain… for years, Colombian
cartels tried to use routes through Venezuela

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.000
to distribute their products.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:38.420
And, of course, to do so, they began bribing
policemen, national guard members, high officials,

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:39.420
etc., etc.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.330
So they’d turn a blind eye.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.440
This was the first stage.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:47.420
As it worked, dealers got to know the land
better and figured out who they could trust

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:52.970
or not, so they moved into the second stage...
something like: “ok, now that we have a

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:58.800
deal, if I give you more money, you don’t
only look away, you also protect and transport

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.270
my merchandise”.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.320
This was the second stage.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:07.420
Later, many Colombian mobsters realized that
given the enormous pressure they had from

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:11.220
the Colombian government and the DEA, they’d
be safer in Venezuela.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:15.510
So at the beginning of the 21st century, that’s
precisely what happened, many of these sinister

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:19.570
“merchants” moved their operations center
from Colombia to Venezuela.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:23.710
And that’s when they started to closely
collaborate with the authorities.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.360
And I mean really closely.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:30.820
What do you think the Venezuelan government
did then?

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:37.460
In 2005, they decided to expel the DEA from
Venezuelan territory and suspend their agreement

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.030
to monitor narco-flights.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:43.560
Therefore, the Venezuelan territory became
a kind of refuge for drug traffickers, the

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.320
United States could no longer keep track of
them.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.400
Fantastic, isn’t it?

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:51.700
Of course, in exchange for getting rid of
the United States, they had to pay a modest

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.520
commission – the regime giants needed to
live off of something, right?

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:56.590
That was the third stage.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:08:01.280
But... just a moment folks, because that's
how we got to the fourth and last stage, which

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.110
is where we’re at right now.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:08.980
Business was going well... so well that many
of the Bolivarian revolution leaders asked

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:10.110
themselves a question...

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:13.990
We have the government, the police, the army
and a lot of resources...

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:16.110
why on earth should we share anything with
Colombians?

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:17.270
Or whoever?

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:24.450
(“We capture them here, we’ve captured
more than 100 Colombian drug-lords, here in

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.450
Venezuela.”)

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:26.450
Do you know what happened then?

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:27.450
Well...

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.331
The Venezuelan authorities began arresting
all the drug traffickers who didn’t want

00:08:30.331 --> 00:08:34.919
to cooperate with them by giving them their
routes as well as their distribution business…

00:08:34.919 --> 00:08:40.770
That’s how people such as Maximiliano Bonilla,
aka “Valenciano”, the chief of the Envigado

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:47.459
Office; Héctor Germán Buitrago, aka “Martin
Llanos”; Diego Perez Henao, aka Diego Rastrojo,

00:08:47.459 --> 00:08:50.639
and Daniel Barrera Barrera, aka “el loco”
fell.

00:08:50.639 --> 00:08:55.499
All of them were found in the list of the
most significant traffickers.

00:08:55.499 --> 00:08:59.370
So everything indicates that right now in
Venezuela, even though there are tons of criminal

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:04.980
groups operating in the area... the government
giants hold the ultimate control...

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:09.449
Characters such as Diosdado Cabello, allegedly
the most important leader of the “Los Soles

00:09:09.449 --> 00:09:13.100
Cartel”, the cartel formed by the top leaders
of the Bolivarian government.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:18.449
(“The Venezuelan people suffer under corrupt
politicians who tighten their grip on power

00:09:18.449 --> 00:09:19.990
while lining their own pockets.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:25.920
“We are imposing costs on figures like Diosdado
Cabello who exploit their official positions

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:31.170
to engage in narcotics trafficking, money
laundering, embezzlement of state funds, and

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.620
other corrupt activities".

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:35.410
U.S. Treasury Secretary Steven Mnuchin)

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:40.449
In fact, one of Diosdado Cabello’s own personal
assistants, Leasmy Salazar, fled Venezuela

00:09:40.449 --> 00:09:42.350
in 2014 with the help of the DEA.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:46.879
And his statement couldn't be more forceful:
in addition to providing evidence on the organization’s

00:09:46.879 --> 00:09:51.370
operation, he stated that Mr. Diosdado Cabello,
president of the National Constituent Assembly,

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:56.269
gives direct orders on the routes and the
departure of boats loaded with prohibited

00:09:56.269 --> 00:09:57.269
substances.

00:09:57.269 --> 00:09:58.439
And he’s not the only one.

00:09:58.439 --> 00:10:01.670
Testimonies are accumulating in the DEA offices.

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:07.699
For example, there’s Walid Makled’s statement,
from when he was arrested in Colombia in 2011.

00:10:07.699 --> 00:10:11.720
Makled was one of the most powerful drug traffickers
in Venezuela.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:15.940
For example he controlled Puerto Cabello,
which according to the DEA was the exit point

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:18.510
for most of the narcotics distributed from
the country.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:23.050
Well, after his arrest Makled declared with
great detail that he had done business with

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:27.560
several dozens of Venezuelan generals, high-level
government officials, such as Henry Rangel

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:32.410
Silva... who was later named minister of defense...
or Hugo Carvajal, former army intelligence

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:35.110
director who supposedly paid him $ 50,000
a week...

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.620
Quite a nice salary!

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:41.379
He also claimed to have financed one of Hugo
Chavez's campaigns in exchange for concessions

00:10:41.379 --> 00:10:44.920
in Puerto Cabello.

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:49.189
With all these relationships, it’s easy
to understand how in November 2016, Efraín

00:10:49.189 --> 00:10:53.970
Antonio Campo Flores and Francisco Flores
de Freitas, two of the Venezuelan first lady,

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:57.670
Cilia Flores’s nephews, were convicted in
a New York court for conspiring to traffic

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:59.740
hundreds of kilos of narcotics.

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:04.069
And, folks, according to current estimates,
business in Venezuela won’t stop growing...

00:11:04.069 --> 00:11:08.569
Between 15 and 20% of all the cocaine that
moves in the world every year passes through

00:11:08.569 --> 00:11:09.569
this country.

00:11:09.569 --> 00:11:14.819
And not only that, apparently the number of
laboratories is rising like foam.

00:11:14.819 --> 00:11:15.819
Of course...

00:11:15.819 --> 00:11:20.279
the giants of the Bolivarian revolution need
money to keep the structures of repression

00:11:20.279 --> 00:11:23.259
loyal: the army, the police, the national
guard...

00:11:23.259 --> 00:11:26.889
Also, in exchange for working in Venezuela,
the different criminal groups based there,

00:11:26.889 --> 00:11:31.459
from the mafia to the paramilitaries and the
Colombian guerrillas, support the regime...

00:11:31.459 --> 00:11:36.439
And since there’s good business, Maduro
and company are still filling their pockets.

00:11:36.439 --> 00:11:41.540
Unfortunately, the consequences of all this
are terrible:

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:47.899
For one, looting all public resources... has
led the country to ruin; And on top of that,

00:11:47.899 --> 00:11:50.040
it’s fueling an enormous amount of violence...

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:53.949
See, according to data from the Venezuelan
Violence Observatory…

00:11:53.949 --> 00:11:57.970
in 2017... there were 89 homicides per 100,000
inhabitants in the country.

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:09.880
That is, more than 26,000 people lost their
lives violently.

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:13.570
Venezuela has become the most dangerous country
in all of Latin America... and the situation

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:16.050
in some areas like Caracas is even worse.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:22.709
The capital’s homicide rate skyrocketed
in 2017 to 130 people per 100,000 inhabitants.

00:12:22.709 --> 00:12:25.829
Meanwhile the members of the government who
are taking advantage of this situation and

00:12:25.829 --> 00:12:30.720
making actual fortunes are buying properties
all over the world... from the Dominican Republic,

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.800
where they are making millionaire investments
in hotels, urbanization, golf courses... to

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:33.800
Madrid,

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:37.459
a city to which not only thousands of Venezuelans
fleeing the disaster are arriving, but also

00:12:37.459 --> 00:12:41.620
many of the relatives of the Soles Cartel
bosses and other high position members loyal

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:42.680
to the revolution.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:48.129
(“I now sometimes find myself sitting in
restaurants in Madrid right next to people

00:12:48.129 --> 00:12:53.230
whom I wouldn’t feel comfortable ever seeing
in Caracas,” Leopoldo López Gil, the father

00:12:53.230 --> 00:13:00.000
of Leopoldo López, a leading opposition politician
who has been kept under house arrest in Caracas.)

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.420
Unfortunately, the Bolivarian regime... has
found its best ally in drug-dealing... both

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:06.980
to fill their pockets and to keep their power.

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:09.740
In short, my friends, that's how things are.

